 "robustness_bootstrap_note": "Wild cluster bootstrap (1,999 reps) applied to every arm AFTER the arms were first run with asymptotic chi-2 p-values. Disclosed as an inference refinement not specified in advance: it applies the SAME procedure the pre-registration fixes for the primary test uniformly across arms, because chi-2 p-values are known to be anti-conservative with few clusters and the arms that rejected are precisely those with the fewest clusters. It makes the arms MORE conservative, not less. Both p-values are reported for every arm; neither is hidden.",
